    "blocks": [
      {
        "id": "p1",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "A solar "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "eclipse",
            "zh": "日食"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " doesn’t happen very often. It’s interesting to see the Sun go dark in the middle of the day. However, it’s never a good idea to stare directly at the Sun, especially during a solar eclipse."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p2",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "The "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "ultraviolet light",
            "zh": "紫外线"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " from the Sun is quite powerful. It can damage your eyes. The sunlight becomes less bright than usual during a solar eclipse. But why is it even more dangerous to look at the Sun during an eclipse?"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p3",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "As the Sun darkens during a solar eclipse, your eyes think it’s getting dark. Therefore, your "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "pupils",
            "zh": "瞳孔"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " become larger to let in more light, just like what they do every evening. Since it’s getting darker, your eyes’ natural protective "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "defences",
            "ref": "v-defence"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " don’t "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "kick in",
            "ref": "v-kick-in"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " as well."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p4",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "During a solar eclipse, there is still sunlight entering your eyes. This sunlight can "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "permanently",
            "ref": "v-permanently"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " damage your "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "retinas",
            "zh": "视网膜"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " if you stare directly at the Sun for a long time. There are no pain "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "receptors",
            "zh": "感受器"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " in the retina, so you won’t notice the damage until it’s too late."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p5",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "However, with a little preparation, you can view a solar eclipse safely. You can use special sun "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "filters",
            "zh": "滤光器"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " that block harmful ultraviolet light. Glasses with these filters can be found at some online stores."
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
